course: dictionary
lesson: 16124
title: Whin: a prickly bush or a hard rock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Whin is an old word, mostly used in Scotland, northern England and Ireland. Many people now call the same prickly plant gorse or furze. «The sheep wandered through the whin bushes on the hillside.» The clues are bushes and hillside, so whin is a plant here.
explain: «Bright yellow flowers covered the whin as far as we could see.» Yellow flowers and prickles are clues that whin means gorse. Check it: put gorse in the sentence instead, and it still makes sense.
explain: Whin also has a second meaning, a rock. «The old wall was built from grey, hard whinstone.» Whinstone is a very hard dark rock. Words like hard, wall and built are the clues that it is a rock, not a bush.
fact: Whin means gorse: a prickly bush with bright yellow flowers.
fact: Gorse grows on heaths and hills, mostly in Britain and Ireland.
fact: Whinstone is any very hard dark rock, such as basalt.
fact: Whinstone was used in Scotland and northern England for roads and walls.
fact: Whin is a rare, regional word. In nature lessons you will often meet the names gorse or furze instead.
exercise: «The whin bushes were covered in bright yellow flowers.» What is a whin here? | A tall tree with green leaves | A small grey bird | A kind of soft cloth | *A prickly bush with yellow flowers
exercise: «The wall was built from whinstone, a very hard dark rock.» What is whinstone? | A soft white cloud | *A very hard dark rock | A type of wooden fence | A kind of bread
exercise: Ella reads an old book about the hills of Scotland and finds «whin». Which word means the same plant in a nature lesson? | Sheep | *Gorse | Oak | Daisy
test: «The walkers pushed through the whin, and their socks were torn.» What does whin mean here? | A loud noise | A hard rock | A field of wheat | *A prickly bush
test: A builder needs something hard and dark to make a wall. Which is the best choice? | Wet paper | Sugar | Feathers | *Whinstone
exam: Which is the best way to work out what whin means in a new sentence? | Ignore the whole sentence | Skip it forever and stop reading | Guess and never check | *Read the words around it and look for clues
